{
  "systemPrompt": "Assume you are a senior HR professional with 10+ years of experience in IT and software roles.",
  "userPrompt": "Task:\nWrite the **CV Summary section** — the single paragraph that appears at the top of the resume, directly under the candidate's name and contact details, and above the Professional Experience section. This is the named \"Summary\" (or \"Professional Summary\") block that recruiters read first.\n\nImportant: This is NOT a simple recap or compression of the experience bullets below. It is an opening pitch: a short, role-specific hook that answers \"why this candidate fits this role\" before the reader sees the detailed experience. Do not merely list or summarise past roles; craft a cohesive paragraph that highlights fit with the JD and (when provided) the company.\n\nRequirements:\n- Length approximately 50 words; sentence count flexible; paragraph must be coherent; no more than 3 items in parallel.\n- When company profile is provided, first and last sentences must be hooks tied to the company; when company profile is empty (JD-only), base summary only on the JD.\n- Match the tone and structure of a professional Australian IT resume\n- Use third-person, factual language (no \"I\", no motivational phrasing)\n- Avoid buzzwords, clichés, and soft-skill fillers\n\nContent constraints:\n- Base the summary strictly on the candidate information in the mapping below (CANDIDATE SUMMARY and MAPPING sections)\n- CRITICAL: Directly address specific requirements and technologies mentioned in the job description\n- Reference specific tools, frameworks, or approaches that match what the JD is looking for\n- Do NOT use generic phrases that could apply to any software engineer\n- Do NOT introduce new skills, tools, or responsibilities\n- Do NOT exaggerate scope, seniority, or impact\n- Do NOT simply repeat or condense the experience bullets; the Summary is a high-level pitch, not a list of roles\n\nIntent:\n- The summary should quickly communicate how the candidate's experience directly matches the job requirements\n- It should function as a hook that shows immediate relevance to the role\n- Prioritize JD-specific alignment over generic professional description\n\nCompany profile (company-specific context; leave empty if none):\n{{companyProfile}}\n\nJob Description:\n{{jd}}\n\nKey Hiring Pain Points:\n{{painPoints}}\n\nMapping (use CANDIDATE SUMMARY and MAPPING sections as the only candidate context):\n{{mapping}}\n\nWrite your response in plain text format in English. Do NOT use JSON format. Write one coherent paragraph (~50 words); when company profile is provided use hooks tied to the company; when empty base only on JD.",
  "temperature": 0.7,
  "maxTokens": 500
}
